{"step_index":182,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T10:29:38Z","content":"The render is finished!\n\nYour video file is located exactly here on your machine:\n`C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\priyanshu readme\\youtube\\Stickman\\stikaman-test\\out\\video.mp4`\n\nOpen it up in Windows Media Player/VLC. This is the baseline for your visual style: clean, intentional, programmatic stickman animation.\n\nNow it's time for the Omni test so we can compare the two paths:\n\n1. Copy this exact prompt:\n   > A dark, moody 2D animation scene. Black background with subtle gray texture. A simple white stick figure stands center-frame holding a large obsidian club — a flat wooden paddle studded with sharp black glass teeth along both edges. The stick figure slowly raises the weapon above its head with both hands. Camera holds steady, low angle looking up at the figure. The figure swings the club down in a powerful arc. As the club swings, the obsidian teeth catch dim red light. The swing ends at the bottom of frame. Hard cut to solid black. Style: minimalist 2D animation, white lines on dark background, no faces, no detailed features. Cinematic lighting, single red rim light from the left. No text.\n\n2. Run it through Google Omni (or whichever AI video tool you are testing).\n3. Watch both side-by-side.\n\nTell me which one looks better for the channel. If Omni looks like AI slop, we stick with Remotion and I'll code the remaining components. If Omni nails it, we switch to an AI video pipeline. Let me know what the result is."}
