al spine (vidIQ's pre-emptive ban thesis + our loophole thread)\n- **New from vidIQ:** Just a Rock in Space (5.26M views), Trust Me Bro (2.77M), Smart Mind Channel (229x breakout), ICRC video (7.4M), German shoe mine example, OPCW AI report, CCW 7th Review Conference 2026\n\n### Honest Script Assessment — COMPLETE\nReviewed vidIQ's full script draft. Key findings:\n- Hook is strong (macuahuitl cold open)\n- Loophole Museum section (5:30-6:30) is best material\n- **PROBLEMS:** \"Here's the thing\" appears twice (banned phrase), macuahuitl \"they banned their own weapons\" claim is historically shaky (can't verify Spanish banned crossbows because of macuahuitl), bat bomb was CANCELLED not BANNED (factual error), \"bans are about power\" thesis is only half-true (blinding laser contradicts it), second half is thinner than first half\n\n### File Naming Decision\nUser asked what to call \"script overview done by vidiq.md\". Answer: It should be called **`beat_map_and_hook.md`** because it contains the 12-minute beat map, hook script, title scoring, and B-roll links.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n\n### Plugin Error — NOW RESOLVED\nA Google Cloud telemetry plugin (`C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\plugins\\googlecloudtools.datacloud_telemetry\\telemetry_hook_bundle.js`) had a broken module path that blocked ALL tool operations (file writes, commands, file reads with IsSkillFile=true). The error was: `Cannot find module` with a double-quoted path inside the module resolution. **User deleted the blocking file** — tools should work now.\n\n### Omni Flash Prompt Requirements\n- Omni Flash generates 10-second video clips\n- Action must be described precisely within the prompt\n- The user has two relevant skills for prompt writing:\n  - `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\omni-flash-policy-bypass\\SKILL.md` — MUST READ before writing prompts. Handles policy filter bypass for weapons/violence content.\n  - `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\ai-ad-prompt-guide\\SKILL.md` — covers universal prompting rules, model-specific guidance\n\n### Remotion Capabilities\n- React-based programmatic video compositor\n- Animates pre-made assets (SVG, images) — does NOT generate images\n- Can: move objects, animate text, compose layers, transitions, render at 4K\n- Cannot: generate stickman drawings, create backgrounds, produce 3D effects\n- GitHub Actions gives 2,000 min/month free cloud rendering\n\n### vidIQ Rules\n- Do NOT call vidIQ MCP tools without explicit permission\n- Always mention credit costs before suggesting vidIQ operations\n- vidIQ web app: Script Writer, Title Generator, Learn, Daily Ideas ONLY\n- User has 5 free vidIQ accounts\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- **`c:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\priyanshu readme\\youtube\\Stickman\\projects\\01_banned_weapons\\research_notes.md`** — CREATED. Full research document (~300 lines). Contains reference videos, primary sources, weapon longlist by era, recommended 14 weapons, overused facts, fresh angles, vidIQ cross-check. This is the main deliverable of this conversation.\n\n- **`c:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\priyanshu readme\\youtube\\Stickman\\projects\\01_banned_weapons\\project_brief.md`** — EDIT PENDING. Line 113 needs `Not started` changed to `✅ Done (Aug 21)` for research_notes.md status. Three attempts failed due to plugin error. Plugin now deleted by user — retry should work.\n\n### Viewed Files (Still Relevant)\n1. **`c:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\priyanshu readme\\priyanshu-agent.md`** (160 lines) — Identity file. Workspace map, channel info, ADHD system, communication rules, schedule. Lightweight pointer file — DO NOT modify.\n\n2. **`c:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\priyanshu readme\\youtube\\Stickman\\implementation_plan.md`** (245 lines) — Main execution file. Production pipeline (7 steps), video priority order (5 videos with scores), tool stack, vidIQ integration, daily schedule, ADHD rules. Lines 83-96: video order table. Lines 33-81: step-by-ste